From facd04e214ab380329c77625eed7f24e8d13a1c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:15:19 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 332/371] pirates: logging out on a ship, at its wheel, at a
 cannon or fixing it no longer closes the game; every ship part tidies itself
 away (crew-0003, client only)

0414 and 0415 fixed DistributedShip itself. On the same logout the server's deletes for everything on his ship arrive
after LocalPirate.delete has removed localAvatar, and the ship's parts and FSM exits still read it:
- DistributedSteeringWheel.delete: base.localAvatar.doId on every wheel delete (AttributeError, the next relog crash)
- DistributedShipRepairSpot.disable / stopRepairing (NameError)
- DistributedPCCannon / DistributedShipCannon.exitFireCannon: combat tray, skill tray, collisions
- GameFSMShip.exitInPosition: localAvatar.getShip()
- DistributedShip.loadZoneLevel(2) shipList and localAvatarExitShip's radar zoom
- DistributedBattleAvatar.hideHpMeter (from disable): an avatar disabled after he logged out

All use getattr(base, 'localAvatar', None) now, as 0414/0415 do, and skip his part when he is gone; with him logged
in every guarded line runs as before. The lane's AST walk of 252 methods reached from the ship and its parts'
disable/delete and FSM exits went from 13 localAvatar reads to 4, all already safe.

Client files only; no AI or UberDOG file imports them. Test: test_ship_teardown.py (real client code) live FAIL 9/18,
patched PASS 18/18; test_ship_logout.py (0415) 4/4 and test_crew_logout.py (0414) 3/3 still pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
